WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.013
The migration runs in six phases:
inventory, coexist, move authority,

2
00:00:06.013 --> 00:00:11.763
bring in the clouds, retire AD DNS
and DHCP, then harden and prove it.

3
00:00:11.763 --> 00:00:15.529
Name resolution has to keep
working while authority moves,

4
00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:17.912
so every move runs the same small loop.

5
00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:22.712
The old system keeps answering until the
new one is proven from every location,

6
00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:25.001
and a failed check just switches back.

7
00:00:25.001 --> 00:00:29.415
The program has planning estimates,
from a day or two up to a few weeks,

8
00:00:29.415 --> 00:00:31.938
but they're estimates, not commitments.

9
00:00:31.938 --> 00:00:35.478
The decision: the DNS
and DDI team closes each

10
00:00:35.478 --> 00:00:39.113
phase on its evidence,
never on a calendar date.

11
00:00:39.113 --> 00:00:41.330
Next, the step you can't undo.
